-- title:
--   Unipotent inertia at q ‖ N, q≠ p, for Hecke–Galois data
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field, let $p$ be a prime with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$, let $N\ge 1$, and let $S$ be a finite set of natural numbers containing $p$ and every prime divisor of $N$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of endomorphisms of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$ — to the residue field of $\mathcal O$, and let $T$ be a complete local noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra, finite and free as an $\mathcal O$-module, with local structure map. Let $H$ be a [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum`](def/CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum.html#L8) for these data: a ring homomorphism $\pi$ from the Hecke algebra to $T$ lifting $\theta$ on residue fields, whose image generates $T$ over $\mathcal O$, such that every $\mathcal O$-valued eigensystem reducing to $\theta$ factors through $T$, with residue field of $T$ generated by that of $\mathcal O$, together with a rank-two free adically continuous Galois representation $\rho$ over $T$ whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials at primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$ are $X^2-\pi(T_\ell)X+\ell$ and whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible. Then for every prime $q\neq p$ with $q\mid N$ and $q^2\nmid N$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $q$ is a non-unit and every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$ satisfy $\operatorname{charpoly}(\rho(\sigma))=(X-1)^2$ in $T[X]$.
--
--   This is the local–global compatibility statement at a prime $q$ exactly dividing the level and distinct from the residual characteristic: inertia at such $q$ acts unipotently on the Galois representation attached to a weight-two Hecke–Galois datum. It supplies the local condition at the primes of multiplicative type used in the construction of Hecke–Galois data satisfying prescribed local conditions, and in the identification of the Hecke eigenvalues at a ramified prime.
